{"parentUuid":"d42f9b69-949f-4448-940c-146905621e7b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3b7d4363-b3fc-44e5-89e6-22ce2e37e594","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TJta4L8XnTQUTqvTes9imy","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\vladi\\.claude\\projects\\C--sources-the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot\\memory\\shadow-diagnostic-method.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"c6f7ea65-bb5c-499e-831c-33f47bde63a8","timestamp":"2026-10-25T15:57:35.427Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"C:\\Users\\vladi\\.claude\\projects\\C--sources-the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot\\memory\\shadow-diagnostic-method.md","content":"---\nname: shadow-diagnostic-method\ndescription: \"How the user wants the Bally The Shadow pinball repair diagnosis run (one measurement at a time, journal file, challenge hypotheses, annotated images of board parts)\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f\n  modified: 2026-10-25T15:57:35.196Z\n---\n\nFor the Bally The Shadow (1994, WPC-S) Power Driver diagnosis, guide exactly one manipulation or measurement per message (where, how, how to interpret), then wait for the result. Off-power checks first, account for charged capacitors, and never suggest powering on before the pre-reconnection checklist is done. Treat the user's recollections as uncertain, never as confirmed diagnoses, and contradict them when evidence requires. Answer in French.\n\nWhenever a message mentions a board component, connector, fuse or test point, also send an annotated image showing where it is (user asked on 2026-10-25). Use the user's own photo when it covers the spot; otherwise annotate the manual's layout (page 2-9) rotated 90° clockwise, which matches how the board is mounted in the backbox (J130 at the bottom, J101 on the right, fuses F101–F105 vertical with F101 left and F105 right). A pre-rotated copy is in `docs/manuel-the-shadow/2-9_PD_implantation_orientee-comme-montee.png`. Draw with PIL, save in `photos/`, send with SendUserFile.\n\n**Why:** the user asked for this explicitly; earlier unstructured measurements did not validate anything, and the Power Driver was already damaged several times. Finding parts from designators alone was hard for them.\n\n**How to apply:** start each session by reading `journal-diagnostic-the-shadow.md` (project root) and the `docs/` and `photos/` folders next to it (manual pages, A-12697 schematic, user photos); update the journal after each significant step (measurement table, hypothesis status, next step). The manual's solenoid/fuse table is wrong for this machine (Sol 01 and Sol 07 are on F104), so map coil supplies by measurement.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":15,"newStart":1,"newLines":17,"lines":[" ---"," name: shadow-diagnostic-method","-description: \"How the user wants the Bally The Shadow pinball repair diagnosis run (one measurement at a time, journal file, challenge hypotheses)\"","+description: \"How the user wants the Bally The Shadow pinball repair diagnosis run (one measurement at a time, journal file, challenge hypotheses, annotated images of board parts)\""," metadata:","   node_type: memory","   type: feedback","   originSessionId: 67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","-  modified: 2026-10-25T10:35:47.132Z","+  modified: 2026-10-25T15:57:35.196Z"," ---"," "," For the Bally The Shadow (1994, WPC-S) Power Driver diagnosis, guide exactly one manipulation or measurement per message (where, how, how to interpret), then wait for the result. Off-power checks first, account for charged capacitors, and never suggest powering on before the pre-reconnection checklist is done. Treat the user's recollections as uncertain, never as confirmed diagnoses, and contradict them when evidence requires. Answer in French."," ","-**Why:** the user asked for this explicitly; earlier unstructured measurements did not validate anything, and the Power Driver was already damaged several times.","+Whenever a message mentions a board component, connector, fuse or test point, also send an annotated image showing where it is (user asked on 2026-10-25). Use the user's own photo when it covers the spot; otherwise annotate the manual's layout (page 2-9) rotated 90° clockwise, which matches how the board is mounted in the backbox (J130 at the bottom, J101 on the right, fuses F101–F105 vertical with F101 left and F105 right). A pre-rotated copy is in `docs/manuel-the-shadow/2-9_PD_implantation_orientee-comme-montee.png`. Draw with PIL, save in `photos/`, send with SendUserFile."," ","-**How to apply:** start each session by reading `journal-diagnostic-the-shadow.md` (project root) and the `docs/` folder next to it (manual pages, A-12697 schematic); update the journal after each significant step (measurement table, hypothesis status, next step).","+**Why:** the user asked for this explicitly; earlier unstructured measurements did not validate anything, and the Power Driver was already damaged several times. Finding parts from designators alone was hard for them.","+","+**How to apply:** start each session by reading `journal-diagnostic-the-shadow.md` (project root) and the `docs/` and `photos/` folders next to it (manual pages, A-12697 schematic, user photos); update the journal after each significant step (measurement table, hypothesis status, next step). The manual's solenoid/fuse table is wrong for this machine (Sol 01 and Sol 07 are on F104), so map coil supplies by measurement."]}],"originalFile":"---\nname: shadow-diagnostic-method\ndescription: \"How the user wants the Bally The Shadow pinball repair diagnosis run (one measurement at a time, journal file, challenge hypotheses)\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f\n  modified: 2026-10-25T10:35:47.132Z\n---\n\nFor the Bally The Shadow (1994, WPC-S) Power Driver diagnosis, guide exactly one manipulation or measurement per message (where, how, how to interpret), then wait for the result. Off-power checks first, account for charged capacitors, and never suggest powering on before the pre-reconnection checklist is done. Treat the user's recollections as uncertain, never as confirmed diagnoses, and contradict them when evidence requires. Answer in French.\n\n**Why:** the user asked for this explicitly; earlier unstructured measurements did not validate anything, and the Power Driver was already damaged several times.\n\n**How to apply:** start each session by reading `journal-diagnostic-the-shadow.md` (project root) and the `docs/` folder next to it (manual pages, A-12697 schematic); update the journal after each significant step (measurement table, hypothesis status, next step).\n","userModified":false,"memdirStamped":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"36dd0e68-9eda-4ada-bd60-1d541c503d09","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/sources/the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":null,"remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]},"error":"not_a_repo"},"live_cwd":"/c/sources/the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d42f9b69-949f-4448-940c-146905621e7b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"session_id":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"golden-gathering-hearth"}
