{"parentUuid":"c935f17b-c95e-4521-8b4a-8e151a08b567","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a34d1881-66f4-4d1d-9060-ce34192f4e36","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018yt76EqdomW4A9tWkPs79T","type":"tool_result","content":"ok","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4d626270-051f-4966-a831-9906bd8f4a3f","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:53:38.827Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"ok","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"910b71e9-7a78-4849-8369-b92957327697","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/sources/the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":null,"remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]},"error":"not_a_repo"},"live_cwd":"/c/sources/the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","platform":"windows"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c935f17b-c95e-4521-8b4a-8e151a08b567","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"golden-gathering-hearth"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","hash":"c02a64d51bb002bbfb6db39c769a5bd248495810e20246de32e7eb748c6d8121","message":{"role":"system","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note: C:\\Users\\vladi\\.claude\\projects\\C--sources-the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot\\memory\\shadow-diagnostic-method.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n7\t  originSessionId: 67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f\n8\t  modified: 2026-10-25T15:57:35.196Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tFor the Bally The Shadow (1994, WPC-S) Power Driver diagnosis, guide exactly one manipulation or measurement per message (where, how, how to interpret), then wait for the result. Off-power checks first, account for charged capacitors, and never suggest powering on before the pre-reconnection checklist is done. Treat the user's recollections as uncertain, never as confirmed diagnoses, and contradict them when evidence requires. Answer in French.\n12\t\n13\tWhenever a message mentions a board component, connector, fuse or test point, also send an annotated image showing where it is (user asked on 2026-10-25). Use the user's own photo when it covers the spot; otherwise annotate the manual's layout (page 2-9) rotated 90° clockwise, which matches how the board is mounted in the backbox (J130 at the bottom, J101 on the right, fuses F101–F105 vertical with F101 left and F105 right). A pre-rotated copy is in `docs/manuel-the-shadow/2-9_PD_implantation_orientee-comme-montee.png`. Draw with PIL, save in `photos/`, send with SendUserFile.\n14\t\n15\tBefore asking for a series of measurements, say in one or two sentences what it protects against (the goal is never to reconnect a repaired Power Driver into a fault), and keep the series minimal: skip values already measured, try the most likely point first. The user questioned a 16-reading table (\"À quoi ? Est-ce que ça me sert ?\").\n16\t\n17\t**Why:** the user asked for this explicitly; earlier unstructured measurements did not validate anything, and the Power Driver was already damaged several times. Finding parts from designators alone was hard for them.\n18\t\n19\t**How to apply:** start each session by reading `journal-diagnostic-the-shadow.md` (project root) and the `docs/` and `photos/` folders next to it (manual pages, A-12697 schematic, user photos); update the journal after each significant step (measurement table, hypothesis status, next step). The manual's solenoid/fuse table is wrong for this machine (Sol 01 and Sol 07 are on F104), so map coil supplies by measurement.\n\n<total_tokens>14995048 tokens left</total_tokens>"}]}}
{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","id":"b02d51b5-75b6-4755-8ae2-310410260c0f","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:53:38.927Z","version":"2.1.310","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"6103e7478104f2c45c04b01fc404a19b39a538f8961fc16524300ddabc9d7e24","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"max"}},"base":"7aefb2b4-ffef-4577-aead-962857946414","keep":536,"tail":["f15ab0e976bd7d3b9368e75d15e90f07341f5909df038f7d60741c583e8aedf3","4a144fe72c988d2ef0a2bfb5ae8d323e058289a9ef08d676c65cdb58917aa94d","c02a64d51bb002bbfb6db39c769a5bd248495810e20246de32e7eb748c6d8121"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",538,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"ea811172b80033453a63ece8ad5ac4eaead4e1c284fa12e014eba002f10def17"}
{"parentUuid":"4d626270-051f-4966-a831-9906bd8f4a3f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"C:\\Users\\vladi\\.claude\\projects\\C--sources-the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot\\memory\\shadow-diagnostic-method.md","snippet":"7\t  originSessionId: 67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f\n8\t  modified: 2026-10-25T15:57:35.196Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tFor the Bally The Shadow (1994, WPC-S) Power Driver diagnosis, guide exactly one manipulation or measurement per message (where, how, how to interpret), then wait for the result. Off-power checks first, account for charged capacitors, and never suggest powering on before the pre-reconnection checklist is done. Treat the user's recollections as uncertain, never as confirmed diagnoses, and contradict them when evidence requires. Answer in French.\n12\t\n13\tWhenever a message mentions a board component, connector, fuse or test point, also send an annotated image showing where it is (user asked on 2026-10-25). Use the user's own photo when it covers the spot; otherwise annotate the manual's layout (page 2-9) rotated 90° clockwise, which matches how the board is mounted in the backbox (J130 at the bottom, J101 on the right, fuses F101–F105 vertical with F101 left and F105 right). A pre-rotated copy is in `docs/manuel-the-shadow/2-9_PD_implantation_orientee-comme-montee.png`. Draw with PIL, save in `photos/`, send with SendUserFile.\n14\t\n15\tBefore asking for a series of measurements, say in one or two sentences what it protects against (the goal is never to reconnect a repaired Power Driver into a fault), and keep the series minimal: skip values already measured, try the most likely point first. The user questioned a 16-reading table (\"À quoi ? Est-ce que ça me sert ?\").\n16\t\n17\t**Why:** the user asked for this explicitly; earlier unstructured measurements did not validate anything, and the Power Driver was already damaged several times. Finding parts from designators alone was hard for them.\n18\