and F105 (the Power Driver schematic is right: F104 → J107-2 Red-Brown, F105 → J107-3 Red-Black) and its solenoid table has errors (Sol 08 is on Red-Black), so map coil supplies by measurement."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b9e2ae34-1ff3-49c4-ae96-7758aece91c2","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgPJbLg2z9D4LFSNuXqTL","requestRef":"b02d51b5-75b6-4755-8ae2-310410260c0f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"4dbde99a-18ba-460b-b6fd-b3a17c7c615c","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:53:44.036Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","session_id":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"golden-gathering-hearth"}
{"parentUuid":"4dbde99a-18ba-460b-b6fd-b3a17c7c615c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a34d1881-66f4-4d1d-9060-ce34192f4e36","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017J1QDDbvQYPmSdeeaxCbrZ","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\vladi\\.claude\\projects\\C--sources-the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot\\memory\\shadow-diagnostic-method.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"057061f3-fa82-4fa8-bcc1-2d71a35d8a10","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:53:44.259Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\vladi\\.claude\\projects\\C--sources-the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot\\memory\\shadow-diagnostic-method.md","oldString":"The manual's solenoid/fuse table is wrong for this machine (Sol 01 and Sol 07 are on F104), so map coil supplies by measurement.","newString":"The manual's fuse table swaps F104 and F105 (the Power Driver schematic is right: F104 → J107-2 Red-Brown, F105 → J107-3 Red-Black) and its solenoid table has errors (Sol 08 is on Red-Black), so map coil supplies by measurement.","originalFile":"---\nname: shadow-diagnostic-method\ndescription: \"How the user wants the Bally The Shadow pinball repair diagnosis run (one measurement at a time, journal file, challenge hypotheses, annotated images of board parts)\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f\n  modified: 2026-10-25T15:57:35.196Z\n---\n\nFor the Bally The Shadow (1994, WPC-S) Power Driver diagnosis, guide exactly one manipulation or measurement per message (where, how, how to interpret), then wait for the result. Off-power checks first, account for charged capacitors, and never suggest powering on before the pre-reconnection checklist is done. Treat the user's recollections as uncertain, never as confirmed diagnoses, and contradict them when evidence requires. Answer in French.\n\nWhenever a message mentions a board component, connector, fuse or test point, also send an annotated image showing where it is (user asked on 2026-10-25). Use the user's own photo when it covers the spot; otherwise annotate the manual's layout (page 2-9) rotated 90° clockwise, which matches how the board is mounted in the backbox (J130 at the bottom, J101 on the right, fuses F101–F105 vertical with F101 left and F105 right). A pre-rotated copy is in `docs/manuel-the-shadow/2-9_PD_implantation_orientee-comme-montee.png`. Draw with PIL, save in `photos/`, send with SendUserFile.\n\nBefore asking for a series of measurements, say in one or two sentences what it protects against (the goal is never to reconnect a repaired Power Driver into a fault), and keep the series minimal: skip values already measured, try the most likely point first. The user questioned a 16-reading table (\"À quoi ? Est-ce que ça me sert ?\").\n\n**Why:** the user asked for this explicitly; earlier unstructured measurements did not validate anything, and the Power Driver was already damaged several times. Finding parts from designators alone was hard for them.\n\n**How to apply:** start each session by reading `journal-diagnostic-the-shadow.md` (project root) and the `docs/` and `photos/` folders next to it (manual pages, A-12697 schematic, user photos); update the journal after each significant step (measurement table, hypothesis status, next step). The manual's solenoid/fuse table is wrong for this machine (Sol 01 and Sol 07 are on F104), so map coil supplies by measurement.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":5,"oldLines":7,"newStart":5,"newLines":7,"lines":["   node_type: memory","   type: feedback","   originSessionId: 67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","-  modified: 2026-10-25T15:57:35.196Z","+  modified: 2026-10-25T16:53:44.069Z"," ---"," "," For the Bally The Shadow (1994, WPC-S) Power Driver diagnosis, guide exactly one manipulation or measurement per message (where, how, how to interpret), then wait for the result. Off-power checks first, account for charged capacitors, and never suggest powering on before the pre-reconnection checklist is done. Treat the user's recollections as uncertain, never as confirmed diagnoses, and contradict them when evidence requires. Answer in French."]},{"oldStart":16,"oldLines":4,"newStart":16,"newLines":4,"lines":[" "," **Why:** the user asked for this explicitly; earlier unstructured measurements did not validate anything, and the Power Driver was already damaged several times. Finding parts from designators alone was hard for them."," ","-**How to apply:** start each session by reading `journal-diagnostic-the-shadow.md` (project root) and the `docs/` and `photos/` folders next to it (manual pages, A-12697 schematic, user photos); update the journal after each significant step (measurement table, hypothesis status, next step). The manual's solenoid/fuse table is wrong for this machine (Sol 01 and Sol 07 are on F104), so map coil supplies by measurement.","+**How to apply:** start each session by reading `journal-diagnostic-the-shadow.md` (project root) and the `docs/` and `photos/` folders next to it (manual pages, A-12697 schematic, user photos); update the journal after each significant step (measurement table, hypothesis status, next step). The manual's fuse table swaps F104 and F105 (the Power Driver schematic is right: F104 → J107-2 Red-Brown, F105 → J107-3 Red-Black) and its solenoid table has errors (Sol 08 is on Red-Black), so map coil supplies by measurement."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4dbde99a-18ba-460b-b6fd-b3a17c7c615c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"session_id":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"golden-gathering-hearth"}
{"parentUuid":"057061f3-fa82-4fa8-bcc1-2d71a35d8a10","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14993540 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"2b0ab537-5689-41a7-a850-056154170306","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:53:44.573Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14993540 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"golden-gathering-hearth"}
{"parentUuid":"2b0ab537-5689-41a7-a850-056154170306","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_017J1QDDbvQYPmSdeeaxCbrZ","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"dd31b6c5-8784-4b26-aa52-3e0fa3e0da2d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:53:53.432Z","session_id":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"golden-gathering-hearth"}
{"parentUuid":"dd31b6c5-8784-4b26-aa52-3e0fa3e0da2d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPJbmZzu8JXDAV4phP9u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Bonne question. Le tableau que je t'ai donné était plus lourd que nécessaire.\n\n**À quoi servent ces mesures.** Savoir quel fusible alimente quelle bobine, ce n'est qu'un bonus. Le vrai but est de vérifier qu'**aucune bobine ne peut détruire la carte une fois réparée**. Chaque mesure contrôle une bobine sur deux points :\n- **sa résistance** : une bobine dont les spires se touchent tire trop de courant et grille son transistor ;\n- **l'absence de contact direct** entre son fil de commande et une ligne 50 V : ça mettrait le transistor en court‑circuit dès la première commande.\n\nCe sont les causes classiques d'une carte qui regrille juste après réparation. C'est exactement ce que tu voulais éviter.\n\n**On peut le faire avec beaucoup moins de mesures :**\n- Les Sol 01, 07 et 08 sont déjà faites.\n- Pour les cinq autres de J130, **une seule mesure par bobine**, vers le Rouge‑Marron. C'est la ligne la plus probable pour les Sol 1 à 8. Le Rouge‑Noir ne sert que si tu lis OL.\n\n## M10 allégée : 5 mesures\n\nFiches J107 et J130 du faisceau débranchées. En ohms, calibre 200 Ω.\n- **Première pointe** sur la fiche J107, position 2 (Rouge‑Marron).\n- **Seconde pointe** sur la fiche J130, successivement sur :\n  - **Violet‑Rouge** : Sol 02 ;\n  - **Violet‑Orange** : Sol 03 ;\n  - **Violet‑Jaune** : Sol 04 ;\n  - **Violet‑Vert** : Sol 05 ;\n  - **Violet‑Bleu** : Sol 06.\n\n**Comment lire le résultat**\n- **Une valeur de quelques ohms à quelques dizaines d'ohms** : la bobine est normale.\n- **Les Sol 03 à 06 sont du même modèle** et doivent donner des valeurs voisines. Une valeur nettement plus basse que les autres, ou proche de 0 Ω, signale une bobine ou un fil à examiner avant de rebrancher.\n- **OL** : refais cette mesure‑là vers la position 3 (Rouge‑Noir).\n\n**Pour la suite**, il faudra compter une vingtaine de mesures du même genre pour le reste de la machine : les Sol 9 à 16, les Sol 24 et 25, les flippers. Après ça, la partie bobines sera validée.\n\nLa session est longue. Si tu veux faire une pause, tout est dans le journal, et on reprendra exactement ici."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":635,"cache_read_input_tokens":703377,"output_tokens":942,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":635,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":942,"cache_read_input_tokens":703377,"cache_creation_input_tokens":635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":635},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"68305521-0676-4401-9515-a68bad019ea9","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPJbkrLAvrDAMmjiZYA4","requestRef":"13c05ea1-78d1-40e2-8238-1d3c3e6a7d76","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"cdddc070-cc9d-4881-a594-f82b910a1e9d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:53:53.430Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","session_id":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"golden-gathering-hearth"}
