{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","hash":"b3cc613edc09db691aadd97f293bda43eb8dae11748a703258cf790594553331","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DEzrW7zPExgPfEWy8Zubgo","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"A-14189 coil pinball resistance ohms lockup kickout\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Coil testing\",\"url\":\"https://archive.maaca.org/s107351202.onlinehome.us/cgi-bin/Blah/Blah2c8c.html\"},{\"title\":\"Coil - solenoid Gottlieb®\",\"url\":\"https://www.marcospecialties.com:443/pinball-parts/A-1496\"},{\"title\":\"Main Restorations Software Audio/Jukebox/MP3 Everything Else Buy/Sell/Trade\",\"url\":\"https://forum.arcadecontrols.com/index.php/topic,14612.msg114339.html\"},{\"title\":\"Coil - solenoid Gottlieb®\",\"url\":\"https://www.marcospecialties.com/pinball-parts/A-4893\"},{\"title\":\"Main Restorations Software Audio/Jukebox/MP3 Everything Else Buy/Sell/Trade\",\"url\":\"https://forum.arcadecontrols.com/index.php/topic,14612.0.html\"},{\"title\":\"Main Restorations Software Audio/Jukebox/MP3 Everything Else Buy/Sell/Trade\",\"url\":\"https://forum.arcadecontrols.com/index.php/topic,14612.msg114099.html\"},{\"title\":\"Coil - solenoid Gottlieb 03-3145 23-635\",\"url\":\"https://test.marcospecialties.com/pinball-parts/A-1496\"},{\"title\":\"Coil - solenoid Gottlieb 22-535\",\"url\":\"https://test.marcospecialties.com/pinball-parts/A-4893\"},{\"title\":\"test.marcospecialties.com\",\"url\":\"https://test.marcospecialties.com/pinball-parts/090-5064-02\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up any listing for part A-14189, so I have no resistance spec for it. The results were general pinball coil references.\n\n- **Marcospecialties, A-1496 (Gottlieb):** a solenoid coil listed at 2.95 ohms, with an optional 1N4004 diode for solid-state games. Reference: A-1496, 23-635 windings, 2.95 ohms resistance\n- **Marcospecialties, A-4893 (pop bumper):** 22-535 windings, 2.1 ohms resistance\n- **Marcospecialties, 090-5064-02 (Data East/Sega/Stern magnet):** Resistance in ohms: 2.9\n- **Coil testing guidance (MAACA):** one source suggests a resistance of 2.5 ohms or greater should be seen on a good coil, and that anything less than 2.5 ohms, and the coil and/or driving transistor may be bad. That threshold is for one coil type, so treat it as a rough guide only.\n- **Lockout coils:** a forum thread about Williams coin-door lockout coils discusses how they work, but it doesn't cover kickout coils or this part number.\n\nTo identify A-14189, check the Marcospecialties product page directly (their URL pattern is /pinball-parts/A-#####), or look for the original Gottlieb or Williams part reference and its winding data in a pinball parts database or service manual.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]}}
