 090-5064-02 (Data East/Sega/Stern magnet):** Resistance in ohms: 2.9\n- **Coil testing guidance (MAACA):** one source suggests a resistance of 2.5 ohms or greater should be seen on a good coil, and that anything less than 2.5 ohms, and the coil and/or driving transistor may be bad. That threshold is for one coil type, so treat it as a rough guide only.\n- **Lockout coils:** a forum thread about Williams coin-door lockout coils discusses how they work, but it doesn't cover kickout coils or this part number.\n\nTo identify A-14189, check the Marcospecialties product page directly (their URL pattern is /pinball-parts/A-#####), or look for the original Gottlieb or Williams part reference and its winding data in a pinball parts database or service manual.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4d5eab08-8d7a-4adb-a3a4-dda0af03037f","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:04:53.173Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"A-14189 coil pinball resistance ohms lockup kickout","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_018mg1qAeHzMYLKVG1LnSnk1","content":[{"title":"Coil testing","url":"https://archive.maaca.org/s107351202.onlinehome.us/cgi-bin/Blah/Blah2c8c.html"},{"title":"Coil - solenoid Gottlieb®","url":"https://www.marcospecialties.com:443/pinball-parts/A-1496"},{"title":"Main Restorations Software Audio/Jukebox/MP3 Everything Else Buy/Sell/Trade","url":"https://forum.arcadecontrols.com/index.php/topic,14612.msg114339.html"},{"title":"Coil - solenoid Gottlieb®","url":"https://www.marcospecialties.com/pinball-parts/A-4893"},{"title":"Main Restorations Software Audio/Jukebox/MP3 Everything Else Buy/Sell/Trade","url":"https://forum.arcadecontrols.com/index.php/topic,14612.0.html"},{"title":"Main Restorations Software Audio/Jukebox/MP3 Everything Else Buy/Sell/Trade","url":"https://forum.arcadecontrols.com/index.php/topic,14612.msg114099.html"},{"title":"Coil - solenoid Gottlieb 03-3145 23-635","url":"https://test.marcospecialtie